-- One-time data migration (2026-11-07): the University Preparation packages for production. No schema change.
--
-- Adds the 24 researched packages of the eight universities shown on /universities (packages/shared/src/university-packages.ts),
-- exactly as `npm run db:seed:universities` would: each subject is mapped to this tenant's offline course by id, else by
-- slug; a subject without such a course stays unmapped (never a made-up course). A package is published only by the
-- publishing rule of presetPublishability: every subject mapped to a published, public course with a group, no course
-- twice, AND its admission requirements verified against an official page (url, academic year, check date, "verified").
-- Everything else is added as an unpublished draft, so nothing unverified can be bought. Prices are not stored: a package
-- costs the sum of its courses' own monthly prices, as everywhere else.
--
-- Append-only: a package whose id is already stored is left as it is, nothing is removed or rewritten; a package is added
-- only when its university is stored, and only with directions that university has. No other site setting, user,
-- subscription, payment, enrollment, course or group is touched.
-- Safety: the stored packages and version are written to "AuditEvent" (action 'content.sync', id
-- 'package-sync-20261107-SiteConfig') before the change; the step runs in its own sub-transaction, so a failure is rolled
-- back and reported without failing the migration. A database without the ILMORA catalog (tests, fresh installs) is left
-- untouched, and running it again adds nothing.
-- Undo: set "SiteConfig".data->'presets' back to the "before" list of that audit row.

DO $sync$
